  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree features intricate, feathery leaves that can be used to teach about compound leaf structures and plant diversity. Its vibrant yellow flowers bloom in clusters, providing a visual aid for lessons on pollination and flower anatomy. Following the flowering season, the tree produces papery, lantern-like seed pods that can be used to discuss seed dispersal methods. The tree&#x27;s adaptability to urban environments makes it an excellent subject for studying plant resilience and urban ecology.",
